# Docker build context filter.
#
# `docker/Dockerfile.server` builds @ponter/server and copies ONLY these paths
# from the context:
#
#   pnpm-lock.yaml  pnpm-workspace.yaml  package.json  tsconfig.base.json
#   packages/       apps/server/
#
# Everything below is therefore dead weight in the context. Without this file
# the context is ~3.4GB: apps/agent/target alone is 2.6GB of compiled Rust,
# node_modules is 809MB, and packages/*/node_modules (api-client, crypto,
# webrtc-core) get dragged in by the `COPY packages/` layer even though pnpm
# recreates them inside the image.
#
# Nothing excluded here is read by the build: the repo has no
# `patchedDependencies`, no `patches/` dir, no `.npmrc`, and no
# `.pnpmfile.cjs`, so `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` inside the image
# resolves entirely from pnpm-lock.yaml.

# Version control
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Dependencies — reinstalled in-image by pnpm install --frozen-lockfile.
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Build outputs — produced inside the image by the builder stage.
**/dist/
**/build/
**/target/
**/.turbo/
.turbo/

# Cloudflare tooling artifacts (wrangler/miniflare)
.wrangler/
.mf/

# Secrets. No .env is ever needed at image-build time; the compose files
# inject them at `docker compose up`.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env

# Local tooling & memory
.remember/
.superpowers/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Docs
docs/

# Workspace members the server image does not need. The Dockerfile never
# COPYs them; excluding them keeps apps/agent/target (2.6GB) out of context.
apps/agent/
apps/web/
apps/mobile/
apps/desktop/
workers/
tests/
scripts/
